To answer your original question: writing a for loop in JavaScript is pretty straightforward:

```javascript
for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
    console.log(array[i]);
}
```

Or, if you want to get fancy with some ES6 syntax:

```javascript
const myArray = [1, 2, 3];
myArray.forEach((item) => console.log(item));
```

